{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223ad7eff6021595657fd1260ccbae48fec13d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = 3\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece4abb664098fa5326858203b59c15c1020fd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1d1cb264d7e17072cb0f6868af22f80180b600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4836c9d877d2d89b7f7cbabd4d532be7c19df2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10)); pair A=origin, B=(14,0), C=(10,6); draw(A--B--C--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, B--C, dir(B--C)*dir(-90)); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, A--C, dir(C--A)*dir(-90)); label(&quot;$c$&quot;, A--B, dir(A--B)*dir(-90));[/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"308\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151e127341dd519bc4db2c3f0774b9554cb3fe52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 33 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }35 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 37 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 39 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\text{not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"547\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe51f2496c9d9e5c4de53fe271ac3739c78c138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = x^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/000eeaf400bfed0e8dcc038c48d98925585e520a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = 3x^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8de132addb225abce5f9dcb9f75c1b28fb258e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\left(180-4x\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd701c0b0dbbe19593e9aef461c64f4b72c7797e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD = x^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810d8e2cc4f15b145bc6e2a281f6d63b078c267b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD = 3x^{\\circ}-x^{\\circ} = 2x^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"202\" height=\"16\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbffe4fdef6962f2364a09cf3bc4b3dd05c161f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CDB = 180^{\\circ}-2x^{\\circ}-\\left(180-4x\\right)^{\\circ} = 2x^{\\circ},\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"19\" /> meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48516899758e4827f95fea1f261ea193ca9fe277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb94e3d043aa1652f6933df7dfc4a760ae51442c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are both isosceles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8fda85df88bfec4f9daf9593c2da46cfc6c9ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = BD$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4764b1f8fc63a3850fdb7135d4a47e291e3410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. In particular, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09a2e16ea6ffcf5c9dbd416626a72ad3707f9ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = BC = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c6047350c97fabbf2f32cdeb9d225948cb0b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = AD = AB-BD = 48-27 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"315\" height=\"16\" />. Hence by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s theorem\">Stewart's theorem</a> on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77bb0086ef01020e7bb3c0010fc29536902c3d34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;BD \\cdot AB \\cdot AD + CD^2 \\cdot AB = AC^2 \\cdot BD + BC^2 \\cdot AD \\\\ &amp;\\iff 27 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 21 + 21^2 \\cdot 48 = AC^2 \\cdot 27 + 27^2 \\cdot 21 \\\\ &amp;\\iff AC^2 = \\frac{27(21)(48-27) + 21^2 \\cdot 48}{27} \\\\ &amp;\\iff AC^2 = \\frac{21^2(27+48)}{27} \\\\ &amp;\\iff AC^2 = \\frac{21^2 \\cdot 25}{9} \\\\ &amp;\\iff AC = \\frac{21 \\cdot 5}{3} \\qquad \\text{(as } AC &gt; 0\\text{)} \\\\ &amp;\\iff AC = \\boxed{\\text{(B)} \\ 35}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"418\" height=\"263\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We apply the law of sines in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486b0a6f49279d4ff79bfaa4f39eed3bdebc1d9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin(A)}{a} = \\frac{\\sin(C)}{c},\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"38\" /> yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d80cbc9439b504d4980424524352ee364f72d91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin(A)}{27} = \\frac{\\sin(3A)}{48} \\iff 9\\sin(3A) = 16\\sin(A).\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now, the angle sum and double angle identities give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd0a51c205dffb8629862a7fc0807d287b9eb21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sin(3A) &amp;= \\sin(2A+A) \\\\ &amp;= \\sin(2A)\\cos(A)+\\cos(2A)\\sin(A) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(2\\sin(A)\\cos(A)\\right)\\cos(A)+\\left(\\cos^2(A)-\\sin^2(A)\\right)\\sin(A) \\\\ &amp;= 2\\sin(A)\\cos^2(A)+\\sin(A)\\cos^2(A)-\\sin^3(A) \\\\ &amp;= 3\\sin(A)\\left(1-\\sin^2(A)\\right)-\\sin^3(A) \\\\ &amp;\\text{(using the further identity } \\cos^2(\\theta)+\\sin^2(\\theta) = 1\\text{)} \\\\ &amp;= 3\\sin(A)-4\\sin^3(A).\\end{align*}\" width=\"498\" height=\"184\" />\n</p><p>Thus our equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd9033f3cb437e3c72ebc4c0dce36e63e78ab86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}9\\left(3\\sin(A)-4\\sin^3(A)\\right) = 16\\sin(A) &amp;\\iff 27\\sin(A)-36\\sin^3(A) = 16\\sin(A) \\\\ &amp;\\iff 36\\sin^3(A) = 11\\sin(A) \\\\ &amp;\\iff \\sin(A) = 0 \\text{ or } \\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"597\" height=\"98\" />\nNotice, however, that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c7779e4765c28049f6938a66bb316d85f7410a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ} &lt; A &lt; 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />, the latter because otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b9980d443ec7b27ce406c37ed284e57575aa9abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+3A \\geq 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />, which would contradict the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/277808a033b0d645b6df93e4ec60050444c8ad88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> are angles in a (non-degenerate) triangle. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e75b03969b9f1b8f1f2a30960dd87467ca92392c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(A) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />, so the only valid solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e3102465b29d1df68180a34e14d9c0789cc9f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(A) = \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6},\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"41\" /> and the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is acute also means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0d6d2ccfd183adb178b8da559afc0d48de8f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(A) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />, so we deduce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a7453fe4670035e1036e1c07b712bf5f41dc3643.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\cos(A) &amp;= \\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)^2} \\\\ &amp;= \\sqrt{1-\\frac{11}{36}} \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"199\" height=\"157\" />\nAccordingly, using the double angle identities again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae0d2e3a41fb8ca6cdb439215b0183ec86f9f02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sin(4A) &amp;= \\sin(2 \\cdot 2A) \\\\ &amp;= 2\\sin(2A)\\cos(2A) \\\\ &amp;= 2\\left(2\\sin(A)\\cos(A)\\right)\\left(\\cos^2(A)-\\sin^2(A)\\right) \\\\ &amp; =2\\left(2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6} \\cdot\\frac{5}{6}\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)^2\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{5\\sqrt{11}}{9} \\cdot \\frac{25-11}{36} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{5\\sqrt{11}}{9} \\cdot \\frac{7}{18} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{35\\sqrt{11}}{162}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"382\" height=\"287\" />\nFinally, the law of sines now gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac99bae73c4827841a884430df785cc91b9e87b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin(A)}{27} &amp;= \\frac{\\sin(B)}{b} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sin(180^{\\circ}-3A-A)}{b} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sin(4A)}{b} \\qquad \\text{(using the identity } \\sin\\left(180^{\\circ}-\\theta\\right) = \\sin(\\theta)\\text{)},\\end{align*}\" width=\"501\" height=\"128\" /> so, substituting the above results, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc40d6e1e35748dd3eb08434926753a9c915682e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)}{27} = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{35\\sqrt{11}}{162}\\right)}{b} \\iff b = \\frac{6 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 35}{162} = \\boxed{\\text{(B)} \\ 35}.\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"52\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174901\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 267/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9479/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.617      1 -total\n 69.89%   13.012      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 28.24%    5.258      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10405:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174901 and revision id 217183. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}